                                                "sense_id": "801032e7-47ff-3adf-8356-46a32e22520f",
                                                "text": "The more strongly people felt about their ideas, the more potent the demons seemed to them: Christians believed that traditional paganism, far from being the work of men, was an 'opium of the masses', pumped into the human race by the non-human demons; and one scholar even ascribed bad reviews of his book to demonic inspiration!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
